SENATE FILE NO. SF0033
Noncitizen driver's license and ID card-revisions.
Sponsored by: Joint Transportation, Highways & Military
Affairs Interim Committee
A BILL
for
1 AN ACT relating to motor vehicles; specifying requirements
2 for driver's licenses and identification cards issued to a
3 person who is not a United States citizen but who has
4 lawful alien status as recognized by federal law;
5 specifying applicability; requiring rulemaking; and
6 providing for effective dates.
7
8 Be It Enacted by the Legislature of the State of Wyoming:
9
10 Section 1. W.S. 31-7-115(a) by creating a new
11 paragraph (iv) and 31-8-102 by creating a new subsection
12 (b) are amended to read:
13
14 31-7-115. Issuance, description and contents.
15
1 SF0033

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0259
1 (a) Upon the satisfactory completion of any required
2 examination, the division shall issue to every qualifying
3 applicant a driver's license, and:
4
5 (iv) The license issued to a person who is not a
6 United States citizen but who has lawful status as defined
7 by title 6, section 37.3 of the Code of Federal Regulations
8 shall state "Not a United States citizen".
9
10 31-8-102. Contents.
11
12 (b) Identification cards issued to a person who is
13 not a United States citizen but who has lawful status as
14 defined by title 6, section 37.3 of the Code of Federal
15 Regulations shall state "Not a United States citizen".
16
17 Section 2. This act shall apply to licenses and
18 identification cards issued on and after January 1, 2026.
19
20 Section 3. Not later than January 1, 2026, the
21 department of transportation shall promulgate any rules
22 necessary to implement this act.
23
